course: dictionary
lesson: 11716
title: Authentic: real, true and honest
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Authentic is a word for things that are real, not copies or fakes. «The museum had an authentic Roman coin, not a copy.» Try the word real in its place. It fits, so authentic means real and true.
explain: Authentic can also mean done in the traditional or original way. «Mum cooked an authentic Italian pizza, using her nonna's old recipe.» The clue is nonna's old recipe: the pizza was made the way it always has been.
explain: The word can describe people too. «Mia is authentic; she always says what she really thinks and never pretends to be someone else.» Here authentic means honest and true to yourself. Swap in honest and check that the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Authentic means real and true, not a copy or a fake.
fact: «Authentic» can also mean done in the traditional or original way, like «authentic Italian pizza».
fact: «Authentic» can describe a person who is honest and sincere, true to who they are.
fact: The noun is authenticity, which means the quality of being real or true.
fact: Copy and fake are words that show what authentic is not, so they are useful clues.
exercise: «The shop sold an authentic football shirt, signed by the team.» What does authentic mean here? | Cheap and very old | Made of paper | *Real, not a copy | Loud and bright
exercise: Ravi finds an authentic recipe for his gran's soup. What does authentic recipe mean? | A recipe that is secret and not allowed | A recipe for a cake | A recipe written in a hurry | *The traditional, original way to make the soup
exercise: «Sam is authentic, so he never pretends to like things he doesn't.» Which word is closest in meaning to authentic here? | Glowing | *Honest | Hungry | Ancient
test: «The guide said the village dance was performed the authentic way, just as it was a hundred years ago.» What does authentic mean? | Done by a robot | Done very fast | Done on a stage with bright lights | *Done in the traditional, original way
test: What is the noun form of authentic? | authentically | *authenticity | authentical | authenticate
exam: Which sentence uses authentic to mean honest and true to yourself? | «The museum has an authentic stone axe from the Stone Age.» | «The shop sold authentic leather bags, not plastic ones.» | «Grandma's authentic pizza recipe has been used for a hundred years.» | *«Jake is authentic, and he always tells people how he really feels.»
